; TLCTC+ Attack Path / Record Notation — Formal Grammar
; Version: TLCTC+ v0.8 (base framework: TLCTC v2.5.1, dictionary
;          tlctc-framework.v2.5.json)
; Format:  ABNF (RFC 5234), UTF-8 source encoding required.
; Canonical prose specification: documentation/tlctc-plus-specification.md
;          §8 (notation) and §10 (minimal grammar, constraints V-1…V-6)
; License: CC BY 4.0
;
; Companion files:
;   grammar/tlctc-attack-path.abnf — core TLCTC attack-path grammar
;     (core §7 notation: sequence, parallel, velocity, domain boundary,
;     transit, intra-system boundary, unresolved steps) with the v0.1
;     free-text BRE extension. Use that grammar for plain core attack
;     paths and v0.1-style records.
;   This file (tlctc-plus-attack-path.abnf) is a self-contained mirror
;     of TLCTC+ v0.8 §10. Use it to validate TLCTC+ records:
;       - record_type = compromise_record   (path with at least one
;                                            cluster step other than #9,
;                                            i.e. at least one direct SRE)
;       - record_type = pure_9_record       (a single #9 step; its SRE is
;                                            induced, no marker rendered)
;     Under core v2.5.1 every cluster step records its own System Risk
;     Event (core §3.4), so the two record types are split on PATH
;     COMPOSITION, not on SRE presence. "+ [SRE]" is the first-direct-SRE
;     marker: a step annotation written once, on the first non-#9
;     cluster step in path order (R-SRE, V-2). The compromise a record
;     foregrounds for reporting is the data-model field
;     reporting_pivot_step, not a notation token.
;     Structured PATTERN/BRE/IMPACT/REPORT codes are required;
;     free-text BRE labels (v0.1) are NOT accepted by this grammar.
;
; Structure (mirrors §10)
;   <compromise-record> ::= <annotated-path> <record-annotation>*
;   <pure-9-record>     ::= <annotated-9-step> <record-annotation>*
;   <annotated-step>    ::= <step> <step-annotation>*
;   step annotations   : + [SRE], + [DRE: ...], [Pattern: ...]
;   record annotations : + [BRE: ...], + [Impact: ...], + [Report: ...]
;   SRE, DRE and Pattern attach to the step they follow; BRE, Impact and
;   Report follow the whole path. <step> and the path operators are the
;   core §7 grammar and are replicated here only for self-containment.
;
; Coverage
;   - Six TLCTC+ tracks: Cause / SRE / DRE / BRE / Impact / Report
;   - Core epistemic annotations on a step: [conf=low], [inferred],
;       generic [key=value]; unresolved steps "?" and "…"
;   - R-BOUNDARY at grammar level: bridge clusters #8/#9/#10 MUST carry
;       a domain boundary annotation in TLCTC+ records.
;   - R-PATTERN-POSITION at grammar level: Pattern is bracket-only
;       (no leading "+"); SRE/DRE/BRE/Impact/Report are additive only.
;   - R-V01-MIGRATION at grammar level: BRE codes are structured
;       (BRE-XXX.YY); free-text BRE labels do not parse.
;   - V-3 at grammar level: the pure-#9 skeleton admits no SRE marker
;       (boundary required, Pattern optional, DRE optional).
;   - V-4 at grammar level (stronger than §10 requires): an unresolved
;       step admits no step annotation at all — no DRE (R-UNRES-5), no
;       SRE marker, no Pattern.
;   - DRE codes are the core v2.5 refinement tree (C, I/Ii/If, A/Av/Ac)
;       with "," as the in-bracket separator.
;
; What this grammar does NOT enforce (validator territory)
;   - V-1: a compromise record contains at least one cluster step other
;       than #9 (the grammar also parses "#9 ||…|| + [SRE]").
;   - V-2: exactly one SRE marker, on the first non-#9 cluster step in
;       path order (R-SRE). The grammar admits zero or several markers
;       and does not fix their position.
;   - V-5: a pure-#9 record carries at least one BRE annotation.
;   - V-6: reporting_pivot_step names a cluster step present in the path
;       (a data-model field; it has no notation).
;   - R-SCOPE (Attack-row admission), R-EXEC, R-CRED, R-SUPPLY, R-ROLE,
;       Axiom VI (single-cluster rule), Axiom IV.
;   - R-DRE-PLACEMENT beyond adjacency (a DRE binds to the step it
;       follows; structured records may link explicitly).
;   - R-BRE-OP-SCOPE beyond bracket fencing.
;   - R-RECOVERABILITY (parsers cannot strip tags and re-validate).
;   - DRE legality on pure-#9 records (only direct-disclosure cases are
;       semantically valid; the grammar accepts any DRE code set).
;   - R-UNRES-8: a path containing "?" or "…" needs a prose note.
;   - Conformance items 1, 3, 15, 16, 17, 18 from §21.
;
; Whitespace: SP is a single space. Records rendered over several lines
; (as in §19) MUST have line breaks normalised to SP before parsing.
;
; Unicode literals used directly in the grammar:
;   →  U+2192 RIGHTWARDS ARROW
;   ⇒  U+21D2 RIGHTWARDS DOUBLE ARROW   (transit operator, core §7.4)
;   …  U+2026 HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS       (unresolved gap, core §7.7)
;   Δ  U+0394 GREEK CAPITAL LETTER DELTA (Δt — velocity annotation)
;
; Parsers that do not natively consume UTF-8 literals should preprocess
; the input or replace the literal characters with hex UTF-8 byte
; sequences (e.g., "→" → %xE2.86.92).
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; =====================================================================
; Top-level record
; =====================================================================

TLCTC_PLUS_RECORD = COMPROMISE_RECORD / PURE_9_RECORD

; -- Compromise record ------------------------------------------------
; A path containing at least one cluster step other than #9 (V-1),
; followed by record-level annotations in any order. The cyber-side-
; dominant vs consequence-side-dominant flavor is observable via the BRE
; family selection, not via record_type.
; The SRE marker is a STEP annotation (see STEP_ANN below); it never
; appears at record level. V-2 (exactly one marker, on the first non-#9
; cluster step) is a validator rule.
COMPROMISE_RECORD = ANNOTATED_PATH *(SP* RECORD_ANN)

; -- Pure-#9 record ---------------------------------------------------
; Exactly one classified #9 step, boundary REQUIRED (R-BOUNDARY),
; Pattern optional, DRE optional (direct-disclosure cases, §4.2).
; No SRE marker (V-3 / R-SRE-9): the #9 step's SRE is induced and
; implicit in the classified step. No epistemic or unresolved operators
; (§8.1). At least one BRE annotation is required by V-5 (validator).
PURE_9_RECORD   = ANNOTATED_9_STEP *(SP* RECORD_ANN)

ANNOTATED_9_STEP = "#9" SP* BOUNDARY
                   [SP* PATTERN_TAG]
                   [SP* DRE_TAG]

; =====================================================================
; Annotated path (cause-side path with step annotations)
; =====================================================================

ANNOTATED_PATH  = PHASE *(SP* EDGE SP* PHASE)

EDGE            = (ARROW / ARROW_ASCII) [SP* DT_ANN]
ARROW           = "→"
ARROW_ASCII     = "->"

PHASE           = ANNOTATED_STEP / PAR_GROUP

; A PAR_GROUP (core §7.1) MAY carry step annotations applied to the
; group as a whole (e.g., "(#1 + #7) + [DRE: Ac]"). Members are bare
; core steps; the "+" between members is the core parallel operator and
; is distinguished from an additive tag by what follows it ("#" / "?" /
; "…" / "TLCTC-" versus "[").
PAR_GROUP       = "(" SP* STEP *(SP* "+" SP* STEP) SP* ")" *(SP* STEP_ANN)

; <annotated-step> ::= <step> <step-annotation>*
; V-4 at grammar level: only a CLASSIFIED step takes step annotations;
; an unresolved step carries none (R-UNRES-5).
ANNOTATED_STEP  = CLASSIFIED_STEP *(SP* STEP_ANN)
                / UNRESOLVED_STEP

; Step annotations (TLCTC+ §10 <step-annotation>): the first-direct-SRE
; marker, a DRE tag, or a cause-side Pattern tag, in any order.
STEP_ANN        = SRE_TAG / DRE_TAG / PATTERN_TAG

; Record annotations (TLCTC+ §10 <record-annotation>), any order.
RECORD_ANN      = BRE_TAG / IMPACT_TAG / REPORT_TAG

; =====================================================================
; Core step (core §7, replicated for self-containment)
; =====================================================================

STEP            = CLASSIFIED_STEP / UNRESOLVED_STEP
CLASSIFIED_STEP = BRIDGE_STEP / INTERNAL_STEP

; R-BOUNDARY: bridge clusters #8/#9/#10 MUST carry a domain boundary in
; TLCTC+ records. This is a profile strengthening over the core SHOULD.
BRIDGE_STEP     = BRIDGE_CLUSTER SP* BOUNDARY [SP* INTRA_BOUNDARY] *(SP* CORE_ANN)

; Internal clusters #1-#7 may carry a domain boundary (rare but valid)
; and/or an intra-system boundary.
INTERNAL_STEP   = INTERNAL_CLUSTER [SP* BOUNDARY] [SP* INTRA_BOUNDARY] *(SP* CORE_ANN)

; Unresolved-step operators (core §7.7). Boundaries MAY appear adjacent
; (R-UNRES-6); core epistemic annotations MAY follow.
UNRESOLVED_STEP  = UNRESOLVED_TOKEN [SP* BOUNDARY] [SP* INTRA_BOUNDARY] *(SP* CORE_ANN)
UNRESOLVED_TOKEN = "?" / "…" / "..."

; Core epistemic annotations on a step (core §7.7): [conf=low],
; [inferred], and generic [key=value]. These belong to the core path and
; survive R-RECOVERABILITY stripping.
CORE_ANN        = "[inferred]"
                / "[" ANN_KEY "=" ANN_VAL "]"

ANN_KEY         = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "_" / "-")
ANN_VAL         = 1*VCHAR_NO_RBR

; -- Clusters ---------------------------------------------------------

BRIDGE_CLUSTER   = "#8" / "#9" / "#10"

INTERNAL_CLUSTER = STRATEGIC_INTERNAL / OPERATIONAL_REF
STRATEGIC_INTERNAL = "#1" / "#2" / "#3" / "#4" / "#5" / "#6" / "#7"
OPERATIONAL_REF  = "TLCTC-" 2DIG "." 2DIG    ; e.g., TLCTC-09.03

; =====================================================================
; Cause-side Pattern annotation (bracket-only, R-PATTERN-POSITION)
; =====================================================================

PATTERN_TAG     = "[Pattern:" SP* PATTERN_EXPR "]"
PATTERN_EXPR    = PATTERN_TERM *(SP* "+" SP* PATTERN_TERM)
PATTERN_TERM    = PATTERN_NODE / "(" SP* PATTERN_EXPR SP* ")"
PATTERN_NODE    = PATTERN_CODE [SP+ LABEL]
PATTERN_CODE    = "PATTERN-" CODE_FAMILY "." 2DIG

; =====================================================================
; Edge / boundary primitives (core §7.2–7.5, replicated)
; =====================================================================

DT_ANN          = "[" "Δt" "=" DT_VAL "]"
DT_VAL          = 1*VCHAR_NO_RBR

BOUNDARY        = "||" "[" CONTEXT "]" "[" SPHERE_LIST "]" "||"
SPHERE_LIST     = SPHERE *(TRANSIT_ARROW SPHERE) BOUNDARY_ARROW SPHERE
BOUNDARY_ARROW  = ARROW / ARROW_ASCII
TRANSIT_ARROW   = "⇒"
CONTEXT         = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "_" / "-")
SPHERE          = "@" 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "_" / "-" / "(" / ")")

INTRA_BOUNDARY  = "|" "[" INTRA_TYPE "]" "[" SPHERE BOUNDARY_ARROW SPHERE "]" "|"
INTRA_TYPE      = "sandbox" / "privilege" / "process" / "hypervisor"

; =====================================================================
; Additive tags ("+" prefix)
; =====================================================================

; -- SRE: first-direct-SRE marker --------------------------------------
; No payload. States where the system first left its owner's control;
; carries no reporting judgement (that is reporting_pivot_step). Every
; classified step records an SRE whether or not the marker is rendered.
SRE_TAG         = "+" SP* "[SRE]"

; -- DRE: Data Risk Event ---------------------------------------------
; Core v2.5 refinement tree (core §7.6; dictionary data_risk_events):
; C; I with refinements Ii/If; A with refinements Av/Ac. A parent code
; stays legal when the refinement is unknown. "," is the only separator
; inside [DRE: ...]; "+" and "→" are not used there (R-BRE-OP-SCOPE).
DRE_TAG         = "+" SP* "[DRE:" SP* DRE_LIST "]"
DRE_LIST        = DRE_LET *(SP* "," SP* DRE_LET)
DRE_LET         = "Av" / "Ac" / "Ii" / "If" / "C" / "I" / "A"
                ; refinement tree (core §7.6): Ii/If refine I, Av/Ac refine A

; -- BRE: Business Risk Event -----------------------------------------
; Structured codes only (R-V01-MIGRATION). BRE_EXPR supports sequential
; (→) and parallel (+) chains and parenthesised sub-expressions per
; R-BRE-CHAIN. The "→" / "+" inside [BRE: ...] are bracket-fenced and
; semantically distinct from cause-side path operators (R-BRE-OP-SCOPE).
BRE_TAG         = "+" SP* "[BRE:" SP* BRE_EXPR "]"
BRE_EXPR        = BRE_TERM *(SP* BRE_OP SP* BRE_TERM)
BRE_TERM        = BRE_NODE / "(" SP* BRE_EXPR SP* ")"
BRE_OP          = ARROW / ARROW_ASCII / "+"
BRE_NODE        = BRE_CODE [SP+ LABEL]
BRE_CODE        = "BRE-" CODE_FAMILY "." 2DIG

; -- Impact: quantified or qualified measurement ----------------------
; IMPACT_NODE optionally carries a label and a "= <value>" tail
; (e.g., "IMPACT-FIN.12 Direct Fraud Loss = CHF 4,500").
IMPACT_TAG      = "+" SP* "[Impact:" SP* IMPACT_EXPR "]"
IMPACT_EXPR     = IMPACT_TERM *(SP* "+" SP* IMPACT_TERM)
IMPACT_TERM     = IMPACT_NODE / "(" SP* IMPACT_EXPR SP* ")"
IMPACT_NODE     = IMPACT_CODE [SP+ LABEL] [SP+ "=" SP+ IMPACT_VALUE]
IMPACT_CODE     = "IMPACT-" CODE_FAMILY "." 2DIG
IMPACT_VALUE    = VCHAR_NO_RBR *(VCHAR_NO_RBR / SP)   ; e.g., "CHF 4,500", "4 hours"

; -- Report: procedural artefact / workflow state ---------------------
REPORT_TAG      = "+" SP* "[Report:" SP* REPORT_EXPR "]"
REPORT_EXPR     = REPORT_TERM *(SP* "+" SP* REPORT_TERM)
REPORT_TERM     = REPORT_NODE / "(" SP* REPORT_EXPR SP* ")"
REPORT_NODE     = REPORT_CODE [SP+ LABEL]
REPORT_CODE     = "REPORT-" CODE_FAMILY "." 2DIG   ; e.g., REPORT-NIS2.11

; =====================================================================
; Shared terminals
; =====================================================================

; LABEL: free-text human-readable suffix on PATTERN/BRE/IMPACT/REPORT
; nodes. Kept restrictive on purpose — operator characters ("+", "→",
; "=") and bracket characters are excluded so the parser can find tag
; boundaries unambiguously. A label never ends in SP, so the space
; before an operator or "=" is left for the enclosing rule (greedy
; parsers would otherwise swallow it). Parentheses are excluded too:
; they delimit sub-expressions inside [BRE: ...], [Impact: ...] and
; [Report: ...] (R-BRE-CHAIN) and no catalogue label uses them.
LABEL           = LABEL_CHAR *(SP* LABEL_CHAR)
LABEL_CHAR      = ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / "/"
                / "&" / "." / "'" / "," / ":" / ";" / "?"

; CODE_FAMILY: the family segment of a PATTERN/BRE/IMPACT/REPORT code
; (FIN, ENT, OPS, NIS2, NCSC, ...). Alphanumeric, starting with a letter.
CODE_FAMILY     = ALPHA *(ALPHA / DIGIT)

2DIG            = DIGIT DIGIT
SP              = %x20
ALPHA           = %x41-5A / %x61-7A
DIGIT           = %x30-39

; VCHAR minus "]" (0x5D) — used for bracketed payloads where the
; closing bracket terminates the tag.
VCHAR_NO_RBR    = %x21-5C / %x5E-7E
